{{Quote|A mythical and more powerful variant of the [[Triple Katana]], using the Legendary Swords.|Item}}
The '''True Triple Katana''' is a {{Mythical}} [[sword]].

The True Triple Katana (aka TTK) is an excellent choice for sword mains in [[PvP mechanics|PvP]], especially when paired with the [[Portal]] fruit, offering consistently high damage, moves that drain [[Instinct]] dodges rapidly, and excellent combo potential. Its moves are also very compatible with air PvP. As a support sword, it can be reliably used to extend combos and trap or catch enemies, especially with the [X] move, however better choices exist as supports. 

For grinding, it is great when paired with [[Buddha]] because of its {{Ability|TAP}} having amazing damage. However, it has a dash on the 4th click, meaning it may be a little annoying when trying to AFK farm with it.

==Obtainment==
To obtain the True Triple Katana, the player needs to get 300 [[Mastery]] on [[Saishi]], [[Shizu]], and [[Oroshi]]. Then, they have to buy it from the [[Mysterious Man]] for {{Money|2,000,000}}. Upon equipping the True Triple Katana, the player will receive:
* {{Title|Demon Eye}} [[Title]] #144
* {{Title|The Hurricane}} [[Title]] #145
;Notes
* The player will not lose any of the previously bought Legendary [[swords]] after purchase of the True Triple Katana.
* Combining all costs (including the True Triple Katana), makes the total cost {{Money|8,000,000}}.

===Tips ===

* Try to server-hop and check the locations without checking the manager if you want the three Legendary Swords.

====Mastery====
* Because the True Triple Katana requires a total of 300 mastery on Oroshi, Saishi, and Shizu, to be obtained (a difficult challenge), a few methods to make the process easier are listed below:
** [[Shop|2x Mastery Gamepass]] is recommended.
** It is highly recommended to refund stats into a sword main and use [[Buddha#Moveset_(V2)|Awakened Buddha]] so it is easier to damage and level up the three [[Swords]].
** [[Second Sea]]: Server hop for [[Awakened Ice Admiral]] or [[Smoke Admiral]], as they can drop the highest mastery in [[Second Sea]]. The player can also grind the [[Cursed Captain]] [[Raid Bosses|Raid Boss]], although this is less effective.
** [[Third Sea]]: Server hop for [[Longma]], [[Cake Queen]], [[Kilo Admiral]], [[Hydra Leader]], or [[Captain Elephant]], depending on the player's level.
** Grinding mastery occasionally and/or constantly can help too.
** A good strategy is also to group up all the [[Cocoa Warrior]]s, kill them, then group up and kill the [[Chocolate Bar Battler]]s while taking the quests for both. This will help in getting money and mastery at the same time.
** It is possible to just grind normally, and mastery can come easily too. 
** You can also use an auto clicker if you do not want to grind manually. (And if you have to do something, you can keep the game running while grinding Mastery, by keeping the auto clicker speed at 750 ms, which allows for a delay before the next hit, so that you don't go ahead on the 4th m1.)
*** It is possible to AFK grind using this trick, however, the player must be wary that without a private server, it is very likely that another player would kill the player, putting an end to the grind.

====Money====
* Since each sword's price is a firm {{Money|2,000,000}}, it is quite difficult to buy them. A few methods to make the process easier are provided below:
** [[Shop|2x Money Gamepass]] is recommended.
** [[Second Sea]]: Grind these bosses: [[Diamond (Boss)|Diamond]], [[Jeremy]], [[Orbitus]], via server hopping. Each server can yield {{Money|75,000}} ({{Money|150,000}} with 2x money) 
*** Alternatively, the player could farm [[Sea Beast]], for their large quantity of money drops, within the range of {{Money|100,000-200,000}}. However, if the player would prefer a more consistent source of money, return to the first given option, as it is usually better to focus on more reliable methods and to only fight Sea Beasts if the player happens to locate one already spawned. (This method is recommended to be utilized in a private server.)
**** Another alternative would be to grind the [[Order]] Boss if the player has enough [[Fragments]] for it. (Not recommended if the player is low level or does not have high amounts of [[fragments]])
**** The other way is to AFK grind [[enemies]] in a [[Private Servers|private server]] with [[Buddha]] or any [[Elemental]] fruit. (not recommended in public servers unless the player is the only person in the server, the server is mostly new [[Second Sea]] players or they check the game often.)
**** Inside the cursed ship, players can maximize efficiency by collecting all major chests before switching servers. The recommended route is:
***** '''Left-hand side room''' → Collect '''6 gold chests'''
***** '''Outside that same room''' → Pick up '''1 silver chest'''
***** '''Kitchen area''' → Grab the '''diamond chest'''
***** '''Right-hand side of the ship''' → Collect the '''final gold chest'''  .
This gives a total of '''9 chests per run'''. This will also give around '''$20-30k''' per run and After looting, the player hops to a new server and repeats the process, ensuring continuous chest respawns and faster accumulation of rewards.
* [[Third Sea]]: [[Sea Beast]] or [[Rumbling Waters]] hunt, as one Sea Beast would give {{Money|100,000-250,000}} without 2x Money, and [[Rumbling Waters]] can give around {{Money|650,000-750,000}} ({{Money|1,300,000-1,500,000}} with the 2x Money game pass.)    You could also go to the other dimension and grind [[Cake Prince]], and the player only needing to do 10%/71k of the damage. It gives around {{Money|50,000}} normally. (This method is not as efficient as the others.) Or they can farm the triple diamond chests at haunted castle as they give 8-10k each. They will have to serverhop each time after, and most of the time it is guaranteed to be there, as not many people farm those chests.
* Another tactic is to simply server hop the chests near the [[Longma]] boss. This is a good tactic and can yield around ~$25k per server if all the chests are there. 

